#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run reproducible Linux I/O benchmarks and archive their evidence.

Configuration:
    JSON object containing server_cmd, warmup_cmd, and measured_cmd.
    Commands are argument arrays, not shell command strings.

Supported placeholders:
    {port}, {connections}, {duration}, {run_dir}, {stats_file},
    {pid}, and {message_size}.

The runner:
    - starts a fresh server for each repetition;
    - waits for TCP readiness before starting the workload;
    - executes warm-up and measured client commands separately;
    - captures server counter snapshots and host state;
    - validates client output when a validator is configured;
    - records failed repetitions and their diagnostic evidence;
    - randomizes configuration order reproducibly;
    - summarizes accepted repetitions only.

Important:
    A run accepted by this script has passed the automated checks
    implemented here. Setup-dependent benchmark requirements must
    still be checked separately before publishing final results.
"""

